{"school":{"dbn":"14K157","name":"P.S./I.S. 157 The Benjamin Franklin Health & Science Academy","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"14","district_label":"District 14","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":393,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"850 KENT AVENUE, BROOKLYN, NY 11205","phone":"718-782-0589","website":"www.franklinmagnet.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/62989","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"Are you ready for an exciting middle school journey? At The Benjamin Franklin Health and Science Academy (PS/IS 157) in Brooklyn, New York, we offer a unique and vibrant learning experience designed to foster critical thinking and prepare students for leadership in our diverse world.  Why Choose Us? - Our Native Garden allows students to engage in hands-on learning about local plants and ecosystems. - In our Makerspace, students can participate in creative projects using state-of-the-art tools and technology. - Our Chicken Coop provides a unique opportunity for students to experience sustainable living up close. - The Spin Room helps students stay active and healthy in a modern, engaging environment. - In our Kitchen Classroom, students learn the joys of cooking and nutrition with hands-on lessons. - We offer a variety of High-Interest Clubs that cater to a wide range of student interests. - Our 8th graders have the opportunity to take the NYS Math Regents exam, setting them up for future academic success. - Our Yoga and Meditation Room provides a tranquil space for students to practice mindfulness and relaxation techniques. - We focus on restorative practices and justice to support our students' emotional and social well-being.  A Diverse and Inclusive Community  Our school reflects the rich diversity of New York City, with approximately 400 students from 3K through 8th grade. We take pride in our inclusive environment, which supports students from various cultural, ethnic, and socioeconomic backgrounds, including 38% English Language Learners and 17% students with disabilities. This diversity enriches our community and enhances the learning experience for all.  Our Mission and Vision  At The Benjamin Franklin Health and Science Academy, we are committed to partnering with students, caregivers, and the community to provide a dynamic and engaging educational experience. Our mission is to meet students where they are, value their unique strengths, and make learning culturally relevant. We emphasize rigorous academic support, emotional nurturing, and social engagement to ensure holistic development.  Community Engagement and Partnerships  We maintain strong home-school connections through monthly parent meetings, workshops, and bilingual communication. Our open-door policy encourages parents to engage with teachers and participate in school events. Additionally, we collaborate with numerous community-based organizations to enhance our educational offerings.  Join Our School Family  The Benjamin Franklin Health and Science Academy is more than just a school; it is a community dedicated to the growth and development of every student. Through our partnerships, traditions, and commitment to inclusive education, we prepare our students to thrive in a complex, multicultural world. We are proud of our accomplishments and are committed to continuous improvement and innovation in our educational practices.  We invite you to join our school family and embark on an enriching middle school experience with us!","start_time":"8:00am","end_time":"2:20pm","languages":null,"subway":"G to Classon Av","bus":"B38, B44, B44-SBS, B48, B54, B57, B62, B93, B98","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Bedford Stuyvesant","latitude":40.6954,"longitude":-73.96,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.89],"n":[183.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":[